    "While I was living in the US, I studied Japanese for busy people, watched VHS video tapes of Japanese TV shows like “Koko ga hen dazo Nihonjin” (“This is what is weird about you Japanese”) which was a TV show where many foreigners explained what they thought was strange about Japanese culture in a panel full of foreigners that had lived for a long time in Japan.": [
      "While I was living in the US, I studied Japanese for busy people, watched VHS video tapes of Japanese TV shows like “Koko ga hen dazo Nihonjin” (“This is what is weird about you Japanese”) which was a TV show where many foreigners explained what they thought was strange about Japanese culture in a panel full of foreigners that had lived for a long time in Japan.",
      "忙しい人のために日本語を勉強し, 日本テレビ番組のVHSビデオテープを見ました  ⁇ Koko ga hen dazo Nihonjin ⁇  ( ⁇ これはあなたについて奇妙なことです 日本人 ⁇ )",
      "Mientras vivía en los Estados Unidos, estudié japonés para personas ocupadas, vi cintas de vídeo VHS de programas japoneses de televisión como “Koko ga hen dazo Nihonjin” (“Esto es lo raro de ti japonés”) que fue un programa de televisión donde muchos extranjeros explicaron lo que pensaban era extraño sobre la cultura japonesa en un panel lleno de extranjeros que habían vivido durante mucho tiempo en Japón."
    ],
